# {{ project_name }}

Multi-app FastAPI project generated by ZodiacCore.

It mounts two independent sub-applications sharing a single database and cache
backend managed by the parent process.

## Endpoints

| Method | Path | Service |
|--------|------|---------|
| `GET` | `/api/health` | parent |
| `POST` | `/users/api/v1/users` | users |
| `GET` | `/users/api/v1/users` | users |
| `GET` | `/users/api/v1/info` | users |
| `POST` | `/orders/api/v1/orders` | orders |
| `GET` | `/orders/api/v1/orders` | orders |
| `GET` | `/orders/api/v1/info` | orders |

## Architecture

Each sub-application follows the standard ZodiacCore 3-tier architecture with
dependency injection:

```
orders/                      users/
├── api/                     ├── api/
│   ├── router.py            │   ├── router.py
│   ├── routers/             │   ├── routers/
│   └── schemas/             │   └── schemas/
├── application/services/    ├── application/services/
├── core/container.py        ├── core/container.py
└── infrastructure/database/ └── infrastructure/database/
```

Middleware (trace ID, service name, access log) is registered on each
sub-application to avoid double-wrapping of requests.

## Run

```bash
uv sync --extra dev
uv run uvicorn main:app --reload
```

## Test

```bash
uv run pytest
```
